      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through the following mechanism:\n\n1. **The Hub never holds the key**: The Hub\u0027s process environment never contains the Anthropic API key.\n\n2. **Local secrets loader**: At startup, a local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file.\n\n3. **Injection at spawn time**: The key is injected only into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts.\n\n4. **No environment mutation**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, the credential cannot be leaked by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only within the short-lived child processes (Ingest and Query agents) that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 2633,
